## graphify knowledge graph (tracked so it travels between dev machines).
## These two hold absolute, machine-local paths — the interpreter path and the
## scan root — and are re-derived on first use. Tracking them would break
## graphify on a machine whose paths differ (the interpreter guard only
## re-resolves when the file is MISSING, not when it is stale).
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root

## Same reason, found in review: these are keyed by (or embed) absolute
## machine-local paths, so they are dead weight on any other checkout. Both are
## cheap to rebuild — the AST pass is deterministic and needs no LLM, and
## manifest.json already carries the ast_hash that drives incremental updates.
## The expensive semantic cache IS tracked: it is repo-relative and cost ~171k
## input tokens to produce.
graphify-out/cache/stat-index.json
graphify-out/cache/ast/
